## FIND-004 note (not a RED/GREEN pair): the 3 affected tests in
## lending-gate-reputation-composition.test.mjs used `if (!base.eligible) return;`, which reported
## PASS both before and after this fix WITHOUT genuinely exercising the composition -- because the old
## fixture used wrong field names (`walletProvenance`/`fundingSource` instead of
## `fuel.provider`/`humanDependencies`) and silently failed isBorrowerEligible every real run. Removing
## the silent early-exit and asserting `base.eligible === true` loudly SURFACED this: with the OLD
## fixture, the sanity assertion itself failed (see below) -- proving the finding's exact concern (a
## fixture that silently never worked). This is the genuine "RED" for FIND-004: not a missing feature,
## but a fixture bug the silent-return had been hiding.

